    <briefdescription>
<para>How a legend draws one row of a series: its label, symbol, color, line, and marker. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Returned by <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1PlotSeries_1a4e5a53df93bf478ae4b3f2f53ee4ff37" kindref="member">PlotSeries::legendEntry()</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1PlotSeries_1a65b522c090eb4baa8377ea2fea24e2ab" kindref="member">PlotSeries::legendEntries()</ref></computeroutput>, and exposed by <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1LegendModel" kindref="compound">LegendModel</ref></computeroutput> as the <computeroutput>entry</computeroutput> role. The line fields apply to the <computeroutput>Line</computeroutput> symbol and the marker fields to <computeroutput>Line</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>Marker</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1LegendModel" kindref="compound">LegendModel</ref>, <ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1PlotSeries_1a65b522c090eb4baa8377ea2fea24e2ab" kindref="member">PlotSeries::legendEntries()</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
